# The EDIT list (TRACKS, EDIT; 14 white keys) and the one track-key rule: white = pick, black = do (MIX and TRACKS alike).
# Each edit is one undo step (hold EDIT); the three erases ask first (press again within 3 s); REC does not edit; nothing erases by holding.
wait 300
tap SAVE
wait 100
tapkey w4
wait 200
expect nev 0
listen
demo
wait 100
press HOME
tapkey b0
release HOME
wait 50
expect events >4
page 11
tap EDIT
wait 100
expect layview 1
shot p42_edit_list.png
# every item in turn: nothing crashes, the text fits
tapkey w0
tapkey w1
tapkey w2
tapkey w3
tapkey w4
tapkey w5
tapkey w6
tapkey w7
tapkey w8
tapkey w9
wait 100
expect textfit 0
# an erase asks, and forgets the ask after 3 s
tapkey w11
wait 100
said AGAIN = ERASE
wait 3300
tapkey w11
wait 100
said AGAIN = ERASE
expect events >0
# nothing to erase: says so
tapkey w11
wait 100
mark
tapkey w12
wait 100
said NO AUTOMATION
expect same 1
# while recording the list refuses
tap EDIT
tap REC
wait 200
expect counting >0
tap EDIT
tapkey w3
wait 100
said STOP REC
tap REC
wait 200
expect recording 0
expect counting 0
tap EDIT
# the same keys on MIX and on TRACKS: white picks the track, black mutes, black 7 solos, black 8 arms
page 3
